{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Fixed root cause of e9d5's CI blocker: change 2436's own new test file (test_payload_shadow_effect_spies.py) had a genuine test-isolation bug -- its effect_spies fixture patched socket.socket.connect/connect_ex via monkeypatch.setattr, colliding with the pre-existing autouse _network_guard fixture (mock.patch.object-based); teardown ordering left connect permanently shadowed for every later test in the worker, matching all 7 CI failures on test_audit_serve_heldout.py exactly. Not a flake -- disproves ticket edeb's hypothesis. Fix: switched effect_spies's socket patches to unittest.mock.patch.object (same safe mechanism _network_guard uses). Added regression test test_effect_spies_do_not_leak_socket_connect_into_later_tests (subprocess pytest run reproducing real file ordering) -- confirmed RED against buggy fixture, GREEN with fix. Local pre-flight: lint clean, typecheck clean, full suite 18419 passed / 8 pre-existing baseline failures (confirmed via clean origin/main worktree, unrelated to this change) / 0 new failures. Amended Gerrit change 2436 (Change-Id I8a032faa9b3fc3ab4d00ce5237541d8a7c7583e7 preserved), re-pushed. Polling for LLM-Review and Verified votes."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788129456493594001,"uuid":"1ad60ea9-e9f4-425f-b1ea-57fca1191fcd"}